 b.summary('A 73-year-old former smoker with approximately 45 pack-years, moderate GOLD 2/B COPD (FEV1 53% predicted, DLCO 36%) and controlled hypertension, dyslipidemia, BPH and recurrent respiratory infections presented with progressive exertional dyspnea and reduced tolerance after discontinuing exercise following rehabilitation completed 26 months earlier. Prior 6MWT/mMRC gains had diminished. He remained ADL-independent with mild anxiety/social withdrawal, lived with his spouse, and had no known allergies, diabetes/cardiac history or relevant family/hereditary conditions.',[ctx,smoke,copd,fev,dlco,*hx,dy,tolerance,old,*oldscores,stopped,loss,adl,anxiety,*social,*fam])
